{#
  The association-role create form.

  **The submit is a `form_row`, where the edit page uses `form_submit`**, and that is not a
  slip: roles/create.phtml calls `formRow($form->get('submit'))` and roles/edit.phtml calls
  `formSubmit(...)`. The difference is visible — a row wraps the button in a form-group div
  and the bare helper does not — so the two pages really do render their button differently,
  and reproducing that is the point of a porting batch.

  The create page is the edit page with a different heading, a different action and no
  record — which is exactly what laminas says too: create.phtml and edit.phtml are separate
  view scripts that include the same fields-partial.phtml. So this template **extends its
  edit twin** and overrides only what differs. What that inherits is the page's assets and
  its inline scripts, which on laminas come from the shared partial rather than from either
  view script, so inheriting them is the faithful arrangement rather than a shortcut.
#}
{% extends 'schoenstatt/role-edit.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate('Create New Role') }}</h1>

{{ form_open(form, form_action) }}
{{ include('schoenstatt/_role-fields.html.twig') }}
{{ form_row(form.get('submit')) }}
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}
